@startuml
title Dromos - Edit a saved route and recalculate automatically
autonumber
skinparam shadowing false

actor User
boundary "Route workspace" as UI
control RoutePlanController
control "Route mutation action" as Action
database MySQL
participant "RouteOptimizer / CalculateOrderedRoute" as Calculator
participant "Google Routes API" as RoutesAPI

User -> UI : Drag/drop, move, add, update or delete a stop
UI -> RoutePlanController : PATCH/POST/DELETE route endpoint
RoutePlanController -> RoutePlanController : Validate input
RoutePlanController -> RoutePlanController : Authorize route ownership
RoutePlanController -> Action : execute(route, change)

Action -> MySQL : load route and existing stop coordinates
note right of MySQL
  Unchanged stops reuse stored coordinates.
  Only a newly added or changed address needs geocoding.
end note

alt Optimized route
  Action -> Calculator : calculate current forced order / options
  Calculator -> RoutesAPI : one road-route request
else Sequential route
  Action -> Calculator : calculate in exact user order
  loop Each overlapping section of at most 12 points
    Calculator -> RoutesAPI : road-route request
  end
end

RoutesAPI --> Calculator : legs, duration, distance, polyline(s)
Calculator --> Action : aggregate result
Action -> MySQL : transaction: update order, legs, totals and polyline(s)
Action --> RoutePlanController : updated route
RoutePlanController --> UI : redirect with fresh route data
UI --> User : updated order, totals and road-following map

note over Action,RoutesAPI
  Geocoding cache reduces address lookup calls.
  It cannot remove the Routes API call required after the path changes.
end note
@enduml

